{{- /*
Per-org model-class routing, resolved from a project's git remote at
project-scope apply time (agentcfg internal/scope Project +
internal/contextres). Each entry's model_classes is a PARTIAL override
merged over model_classes.yaml's defaults, so a context only names the
classes it actually changes.

WHY THIS EXISTS: cloud API keys are billed to an account that personal
work must not touch, so personal repos have to run against the local mlx
server. That separation is a billing boundary, not a preference. This
file is the single declarative statement of it.

Previously the same routing lived in dot_local/bin/executable_aoe-model-class's
jq, which reimplemented org matching by parsing `git remote get-url origin`
and wrote .omp/config.yml itself. agentcfg models it natively now, so the
hook only invokes `agentcfg apply --scope project` and there is one writer
per file — the same two-writer hazard
.chezmoiscripts/run_onchange_after_agentcfg-apply.sh.tmpl documents for
opencode.json applies here too.

RENDERED FROM local.yaml, NOT COMMITTED LITERALLY: org names are the same
untracked `orgs.<org>.model_class` data local.yaml.example documents, read
straight from `chezmoi data` the way dot_agents/prompts/lead.md and
dot_config/kb/collectors/gh.md already read orgs.<org>.issues. This repo is
public; no org name reaches git from here.

The local model's small context window is what makes mcp_servers.yaml's
exclude_for_models necessary — see that file's header. Routing a context's
`default` class to the local model WITHOUT those exclusions does not work:
omp mounts every targeted MCP server into its primary session
unconditionally (agentcfg ADR-0002) and their combined tool schemas exceed
the local window outright, so omp silently falls back to a cloud model and
the boundary this file draws is breached with no error anywhere.

git_remote_host is github.com for every org here; agentcfg treats an unset
match key as a wildcard, but pinning it keeps a same-named org on another
forge from matching by accident.
*/ -}}
{{- /* hasKey, not `.orgs | default dict`: chezmoi errors on a missing key
       before the pipe runs, so a machine whose local.yaml omits orgs
       entirely would fail every apply. Same guard style as
       dot_omp/private_agent/models.yml.tmpl's .local_model check. */ -}}
{{- $orgs := dict -}}
{{- if hasKey . "orgs" -}}{{- $orgs = .orgs -}}{{- end -}}
{{- $entries := dict -}}
{{- range $org, $cfg := $orgs -}}
{{-   if hasKey $cfg "model_class" -}}
{{-     $entries = set $entries $org (index $cfg "model_class") -}}
{{-   end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- if not $entries -}}
contexts: []
{{- else -}}
contexts:
{{- range $org := (keys $entries | sortAlpha) }}
  - match:
      git_remote_host: github.com
      git_remote_owner: {{ $org }}
    model_classes:
{{- range $class := (keys (index $entries $org) | sortAlpha) }}
      {{ $class }}: {{ index (index $entries $org) $class }}
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
